 "plain": "YEAH! Then stack a hundun… yeah…\nYeah… A good friend once told me\n“First get yo monyon… then stack a hundun.”\n\nHe said “First get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun”\n\nI’m the dealer for the whole tribe.\nAlabama to the coastline.\nWe the family we got soul ties.\nBy your side just like roadside.\n\nI drive a VW used to drive a Nissan\nReprogram it if you lose a keyfob….\nAYE! Don’t loose the keyfob.\nHomie this a 2015 it’s a beater.\nYou don’t know what I been through.\nWhat you tryna get into?\nHe mental. Ran off with the rental\nGot spun like a spindle.\nPull up with the hitcrew…\nPulled up with the hit crew.\nWhat she wrote was so simple;\n\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\n\nYou already know you already know\nIf you need to get equipped with a whip, Call whip equipped send a little dough\nIt’s a foundation we gon’ build it slow send a little dough send a little dough\nIt’s a foundation we gon’ build it slow… Yeah!\nCame from the dirt the mud had to get it out the sand too\nI was walking with my people like Jesus in his sandals\nNoah how I turn the tide wait, Moses how I turn the tide now\nMotion like I’m burning tires. If you know me .I’mmoa bring the tribe out ARGH!\n\nI’m the dealer for the whole tribe (WOO!)\nAlabama to the coastline (WOO!)\nWe the family we got soul ties (WOO!)\nBy your side just like roadside\n\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun\nFirst get your monyon. Then stack a hundun",
